# Goat OS AI Routing

Use the repo's local AI setup before broad code or docs scans.

## Local Setup

Run from the repository root:

```bash
make ai-setup
make ai-rebuild AI_BACKEND=auto
make ai-doctor
```

Generated graph artifacts are local-only and must not be committed:

- `.code-review-graph/`
- `graphify-out/graph.json`
- `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md`
- `graphify-out/graph.html`
- `graphify-out/manifest.json`
- `graphify-out/cost.json`
- `graphify-out/cache/`

## Routing

| Task shape | First move |
| --- | --- |
| Cold orientation, review, or diff | CRG minimal context, then one targeted graph query |
| Known symbol traversal | CRG callers/callees/imports/tests query directly |
| Keyword/domain lookup | CRG semantic search, then targeted graph query |
| Docs/product question | Graphify query against local `graphify-out/graph.json` |
| Single file/function body | Read the file directly; use graph only for impact |
| HTTP routes, config, SQL strings, uncommitted code | Native grep/read |

Cursor project hooks live in `.cursor/hooks.json` and reuse `tools/agent-hooks/`
(graph-first guard, RTK, write-scope, post-edit contract checks). Restart Cursor
after hook edits if they do not load. Run `make ai-doctor` after setup and after
AI-tooling edits.
